+- VERIFIED: rc.5 manifest `b6f56aac…04c`, tree `e6a13215…2fae`, 448 files, repository-level conformance status 3 modified + 354 untracked; `main=origin/main=17804ce`; committed pin `00b1688a…e967`; 23-file candidate product delta remains `_test.go`-only. The current no-Go/no-Windows harness independently produced `ALL 41 EXPECTATIONS MET`, real exit 0.
+- FINDING: §5.0 packs three environment assignments into scalar `E`, and §9.2 packs `make` plus `GOROOT_EXPECTED` into scalar `MK`. The required project shell is zsh, which does not field-split scalar expansions: T-P1 silently sets a malformed `GOROOT` while leaving `GOTOOLCHAIN`/`GOENV` unset, and every `$MK` gate exits 127 as a command-not-found. The `/bin/sh`-only harness did not cover either operator-facing command.
+- FINDING: revision 6 names `TASK-260729-osjeay_verify-recipes.sh` as its 41-case resource, but that board resource is the historical 21-case script (`65a02fbe…e5a`); the actual 41-case script is `TASK-260729-osjeay_verify-recipes-cycle5.sh` (`fcb11c56…9f9`).
+- FINDING: §5.3 still describes the Linux prerequisite as Go 1.25.x despite the exact-go1.25.5 invariant and gate.
